        <body>
            <div xml:id="d630">

                <pb facs="0819" n="809" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg809"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.24/3–447: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Belgium</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-03-04T21:00:00+01:00">March 4, 1947—9
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 4—8:48 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>329. When your 223, February 24 was received, Spaak was in Paris, but he [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">we?</hi>] outlined problem to Loridan,<anchor n="54"
                        xml:id="d630-f1"/> who said he would discuss it with Spaak upon latter’s
                    return. I raised it with Spaak this afternoon. He states that, due insignificant
                    Belgian domestic arms market, Fabrique Rationale lives by exports. Inasmuch as
                    Chinese Government was fully recognized friendly and one of principal allies in
                    war, he would find it very difficult vis-à-vis both Chinese Government and
                    Fabrique Rationale to obstruct such sale in absence of specific international
                    agreement not to sell arms to China. In view tenor of your telegram, I did not
                    press him, and while he indicated willingness to examine matter further upon his
                    return from Praha next week, should we press him to do so, I received distinct
                    impression he hoped we would not.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d630-f1" n="54" xml:id="d630-f1-content">
                <p>Walter Loridan, secretary to the Belgian Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
